                <pb facs="0322" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/717: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-03T11:00:00+07:00">April 3, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 3—3:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. The Foreign Office has been approached by the Japanese press for a statement
                    in regard to Wang Ching Wei government. Reply will be non-committal. The Prime
                    Minister told me today that this country will not have relations with it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
